SEMI_JUDGING = (
    "Everything is judged on labelled rows the method was never allowed to see, against the *same base learner trained on the real labels alone* "
    "(`supervised_only_baseline`, `gain_over_supervised`, `verdict`). A semi-supervised method that does not beat its own base learner is not helping, "
    "however many rows it labelled. Read the gain against the test-set standard error the tool reports: with a few dozen held-out labels, a gain of "
    "one or two points is noise. When the data carries a truth column for the unlabelled rows, the audit of the pseudo-labels (`accuracy_vs_truth`, "
    "by confidence band) is the most direct evidence of whether the method labels rows correctly; without it, the held-out gain is all there is."
)

